        history:"Shin Buddhism's founder Shinran taught salvation through simple gratitude — which made it the faith of ordinary people. The Founder's Hall (rebuilt 1895 after fire) was raised partly with ropes woven from hair donated by female believers; a coil is displayed inside.",
